Traversal simply means:

Going through the elements of an array/list one by one.

For example:

numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40]

Traversal means visiting:

10 → 20 → 30 → 40
Method 1 — Directly get each value
for num in numbers:
    print(num)

This is usually the cleanest way when you only need the values. easiest way 

Method 2 — Use the index
for i in range(len(numbers)):
    print(numbers[i])

Here you're working with the index.

This is useful when you need to modify elements or compare an element with another element using indices. 

Example

Suppose:

numbers = [5, 8, 2, 9]

We want to print every element.

for num in numbers:
    print(num)

Output:

5
8
2
9

Complexity:

Time → O(n)
Extra space → O(1)


Why space O(1)?

Because we're not creating another array containing n elements. We're just using one variable, num.
